# any nested per-subproject venv (e.g. research/neuromorphic_torch/.venv-neuro)
**/.venv-*/
# The four below are ALREADY covered by the `**/.venv-*/` glob above for git's
# purposes and are listed redundantly for graphify, which honours explicit
# directory lines but not the `**/` prefix form. Measured 2026-08-07: exactly
# these four leaked 651 nodes into graphify-out/graph.json (.venv-lake-py311
# alone contributed 635, which is why `graphify query "k largest values"`
# answered with bottle.py from a vendored web framework). graphify's own
# _SKIP_DIRS (detect.py:651) matches ".venv" exactly and *_venv/*_env by
# suffix, so a `.venv-` PREFIX variant is never pruned by it either.
.venv-arc/
.venv-build/
.venv-lake-gil/
.venv-lake-py311/
venv/
env/

